  {
   "t": 1791260094.150454,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "Submitted. Summary of my approach:\n\n1. **Declared triggers upfront** (before any moves): stop if best-so-far Sharpe exceeds 1.2, stop after 4 failures, or stop if the last gain from a move is \u22640.02. This fixed my stopping discipline before seeing any data.\n\n2. **`init`**: anchored on the single best feature out of 80 candidates (including sign flips), yielding in-sample Sharpe **1.2151**.\n\n3. Since this immediately cleared my pre-declared `best_so_far_above(1.2)` bar, I invoked `stop` on that trigger \u2014 a valid, pre-committed stopping rule, so the whole (very short) search remains replayable/non-adaptive.\n\n4. **Final specification**: single feature (feature index 0, as selected by `init`, sign as returned), equal-weight (trivially, since it's just one feature), held long/short per the harness's internal sign choice.\n\n5. **Predicted OOS Sharpe**: mean 0.55, sd 0.45 \u2014 reflecting that even a single best-of-80 selection carries meaningful selection bias, so I haircut the in-sample 1.21 substantially while keeping wide uncertainty bands given the small number of moves and the inherent noise in Sharpe estimation."
